<title>FINLAND: Neste says EU to co-fund gas grid study.</title>
<headline>Neste says EU to co-fund gas grid study.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish oil and energy group Neste Oy said in a statement on Tuesday the European Union would co-finance a consortium feasibility study of a Nordic Gas Grid, which Neste is coordinating.</p>
<p>&quot;The feasibility study has a total budget of Ecu 1.2 million (seven million markka), half of which will be financed by the EU and the remainder by the consortium,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The consortium consists of Vattenfall Naturgas AB, Sydgas AB, Goteborg Energi AB and Mellansvenska Naturgaskonsortiet AB from Sweden, Dansk Naturgas A/S from Denmark and Neste Oy and Gasum Oy from Finland, it added.</p>
<p>&quot;The study will examine the possibility of developing and linking up the natural gas networks of Norway, Denmark, Sweden, Finland, Russia and the Baltic States,&quot; Neste said.</p>
<p>The project was officially included on the list of Trans-European Energy Networks (TEN-Energy) on June 11, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
